Let AEC3's linear filter learn through music beside an unchanged reference, mixing per bin

At a call's start with music on the other side, AEC3 keeps using a linear filter that
does not cancel the music for several seconds, and the music comes back to them for 2 to
8 s. Music often leaves the render signal poorly excited (RenderSignalAnalyzer's
PoorSignalExcitation: a few strong narrow bands), and while it is, the refined filter's
gain (RefinedFilterUpdateGain) does not update at all, for size_partitions blocks after
the last poorly excited one. An earlier candidate, using the linear filter only after
sustained convergence, cut the music's echo but held a headset user's first words down
longer, and was dropped. This one leaves headsets, voice, unmute and output changes as
they are by keeping upstream's chain beside the new one and choosing, per frequency bin,
between their outputs.

The refined filter may now learn through poor excitation
(RefinedFilterUpdateGain::SetLearnWithPoorExcitation, Subtractor::SetLearnWithPoorExcitation,
which passes it on before each Compute; off by default): poor excitation then does not
reset the counter that holds the update back, and the step size mu is halved while poor
excitation was seen within the last size_partitions blocks (a new counter of blocks since
it was last seen, kept also while learning through it, set as the old counter at an echo
path change). The narrow bands stay masked as before (MaskRegionsAroundNarrowBands).
AecState::FilterConvergenceSeen tells whether a converged filter (SubtractorOutputAnalyzer's
any_filter_converged: the refined filter, or the coarse one by the strict criterion) has
been seen since the filter quality analyzer's last reset (a delay change: a call's start,
a restart for recording or for other devices, a new delay).

EchoRemoverImpl, with one capture channel and no neural residual echo estimator, now runs
a second, complete chain (ReferenceChain: its own Subtractor, AecState,
RenderSignalAnalyzer, ResidualEchoEstimator without the neural estimator, SuppressionGain
and ComfortNoiseGenerator) making exactly upstream's calls on the same capture, render and
echo path variability (capture saturation, HandleEchoPathChange, SetInitialState,
TransitionTriggered, Update, comfort noise from E2 when the linear estimate was usable
before the Update), and never learning the new way: it gives what upstream gives, sample
for sample, so patches 0010 to 0016 (recording_restarted, the kept transparent mode,
RestartForOtherDevices) act on both chains alike. The first chain learns through poor
excitation when a converged filter has been seen since its last reset and the previous
block was not dominated by the near end (SuppressionGain::IsDominantNearend). Both
chains' linear errors are smoothed per bin with 0.3: ev the first chain's E2, not bounded
by Y2; em the reference's E2 as upstream gives it to its suppressor (bounded by Y2 while
its linear estimate is usable). Per bin, the output (the gain on the linear output, or on
the capture, with the comfort noise of the chain chosen):
  ev > 1.5 em: the reference's;
  ev > 0.7 em: the higher of the two in power, the first chain's capped at 4 times the
    reference's by lowering its gain;
  otherwise: the lower of the two.
The high bands take the same rule from the sums of ev and em over bins 1 to 15: the
reference's gain, the higher or the lower of the two gains, with that chain's high band
comfort noise. One ApplyGain then forms the output from the mixed spectrum, gains and
comfort noise.

With more than one capture channel, or a neural residual echo estimator, there is no
reference chain and the echo remover is upstream's, the first chain never learning the
new way. The echo controller's metrics and the linear output it exports are the first
chain's (with the mixed gains for the metrics). Everything the reference needs is
allocated with the echo remover; it costs a second AEC3 echo remover's work on the
capture thread.

Constants: smoothing of the errors 0.3; ratios 1.5 (reference) and 0.7 (higher or lower);
cap 4 times the reference's power; high bands' decision from bins 1 to 15; mu halved for
size_partitions blocks after poor excitation.

Measured: not yet.
